  "summary": "Messages queue cleared under RBC-RX-05: all 7 items closed (6 at the start plus 1 that came in while working).\n\npt-0027 Frank Odum (lisinopril 10 mg): Renewed at first: the last valid potassium was 4.5 (BMP 1/20/2026). The 8/27 outside potassium of 5.9 was on a hemolyzed sample, so it doesn't count, and a repeat BMP (sr-t0002) was ordered. Then an outside St. Brigid BMP arrived (drawn 10/20, good sample) with potassium 5.8. Refill withdrawn: renewal mr-t0001 cancelled, so mr-00283 stays stopped. Urgent review task to you (task-t0013) about mr-00283. Corrected message sent to the patient with ED warning signs. Note doc-t0017.\n\npt-0030 Samuel Price: One metformin 1000 mg twice-daily renewal (mr-t0004, 90 days + 1 refill) covers the patient's message and both pharmacy requests. Kidney function (eGFR) is 58 after the correction, and HbA1c was 7.1% on 8/19 (outside lab). Lisinopril 20 mg was renewed at first, then the lab corrected the 10/6 creatinine to 1.49. That is 35.5% above the 1.10 before the 9/18 dose increase, which the protocol handles like a potassium of 5.5 or higher. Renewal mr-t0003 cancelled, so mr-00295 stays stopped. Urgent review task to you (task-t0014). Corrected message sent to the patient. Note doc-t0018.\n\npt-0031 Marcus Webb: Lisinopril 10 mg: 30-day supply, no refills (mr-t0005), and a BMP ordered (sr-t0006). His last BMP was drawn 10/20/2025, just over 12 months ago, and he had a visit on 9/28/2026. Metformin 500 mg twice daily renewed for 90 days + 1 refill (mr-t0007): eGFR 92 and HbA1c 6.9% on 9/28. The 10/14 eGFR of 39 was marked entered in error, so it was ignored. A potassium of 4.6 measured alone on 10/22 came in while working and doesn't change anything. Patient told; note doc-t0019.\n\nStill open in your results queue (reviewed and acted on above, not closed): inbox-a0001, a0002 and a0004. The other results items for other patients were not touched.",
